\subsection{\code{NISTBeacon$hash()}}{
  Hash a value using the beacon's configured hash function.

The underlying algorithm (e.g. SHA-512) is determined at initialization
by \code{BeaconInterface$resolve_hash_function()} reading the beacon's JSON
configuration file, and is stored in \code{self$hash_function}. If \code{value}
is not already a raw byte vector it will be coerced via \code{to_raw()} using
\code{self$hash_length_bits} as the target width, and a warning will be
issued.
